==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|tendrillon||bud, shoot, cartilage}}, perhaps a diminutive of {{m|frm|tendron||cartilage}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|tendre||soft}} (see [[tender]] (adj.)), or else from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|tendere||to stretch, extend}} (see [[tender]] (v.)).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛn.dɹəl/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|botany}} A thin, [[spirally]] [[coiling]] [[stem]] that attaches a [[plant]] to its [[support]].
# {{lb|en|zoology}} A [[hair]]-like [[tentacle]].

